    "q-68973": {
      "dom_id": "step-q68973",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "$\\frac{3}{5\\sqrt{3}}=$",
      "worked_solution": "To remove the radical $\\sqrt{3}$ from the denominator, all we need to do is multiply both the numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{3}$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5\\sqrt{3}} & = \\\\ \\frac{3}{5\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}} & = \\\\ \\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{5\\cdot (\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{5\\cdot 3} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5} & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
