    "q-68978": {
      "dom_id": "step-q68978",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{7}}=$",
      "worked_solution": "To remove the radical $\\sqrt{7}$ from the denominator, all we need to do is multiply both the numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{7}$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{7}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{7}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{7}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{7}}{(\\sqrt{7})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{7}}{7} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the product rule to simplify the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{7}}{7} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3\\cdot 7}}{7} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{7} & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
